<title>TURKEY: Turk Garanti Bank doubles 9-mth net.</title>
<headline>Turk Garanti Bank doubles 9-mth net.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	  667.70  vs     767.35</p>
<p>    Net profit			12,018.56  vs   6,138.79</p>
<p>    Net interest income	   27,355.84  vs  12,695.70</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense    13,935.06  vs   5,036.91</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans	  28.97  vs	 0</p>
<p>    Loans			    165,994.93  vs  58,459.23</p>
<p>    Deposits			 165,206.36  vs  69,979.21</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		  81,192.06  vs  31,348.71</p>
<p>    Equity			    26,851.68  vs  11,900.50</p>
<p>    Capital			   18,000.00  vs   8,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Garanti Bankasi A.S., a leading Turkish commercial bank, is largely owned by financial and commercial group Dogus group.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
